  "id": "DrugBank_DB01590 - MONDO_7763",
  "verbalization": "Everolimus, a mTOR inhibitor, is linked to Nonpapillary Renal Cell Carcinoma through a chain of indications that involve Renal Cell Adenocarcinoma, which in turn is indicated for Tivozanib, Axitinib, and Sirolimus. This suggests a potential pathway where Everolimus may influence the progression or treatment of Renal Cell Adenocarcinoma, which then interacts with other drugs to affect Nonpapillary Renal Cell Carcinoma. The recurring mechanism involves the use of mTOR inhibitors in the treatment of renal cell carcinomas, with Everolimus being a key player in this context. The evidence supports a possible dependency on mTOR signaling pathways in the development or progression of Nonpapillary Renal Cell Carcinoma, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these indications highlights the role of Everolimus in the broader context of renal cell carcinoma treatment, emphasizing its potential as a therapeutic agent in this disease.",
